Ethernet -Collection of Network protocols and standards.

Unshielded Twisted Pair Cables (UTP)
These are copper cables used in Ethernet Standards.
They have no metallic shield, making them vulnerable to electrical interference.
Support distances upto 100m.

Full duplex transmissions means both pins will send and receive data at the same time
and no problems eg collisions will occur because separate wires to send and receive data.

Straight Through Cable
A copper cable has two RJ-45 connectors one on each end.
They are called so since Pin 1 connects to Pin 1, Pin 2 to Pin 2 etc.

Crossover Cable
Connects Pin 1 to Pin 3
